@startuml
title logGO - cmd/server Component Overview

left to right direction

actor Browser
actor "Pushing client\n(any protocol)" as Pusher
cloud "Any remote instance\nshaped like conTogether" as Remote

package "logGO process" {
  component "HTTP mux" as Mux
  component "internal/webui" as WebUI
  component "internal/sources.Registry" as Registry
  component "internal/ingest\n(one goroutine per\nPULL source)" as Ingest
  component "ingest_handlers.go\n(REST+WS+gRPC push)" as PushHandlers
  component "logGO.Manager" as Manager
  file "logGO.log" as LogFile
  file "sources.json" as SourcesFile
}

Browser --> Mux
Pusher --> Mux
Mux --> WebUI
Mux --> Registry
Mux --> PushHandlers
Mux --> Manager

Registry --> SourcesFile : persist
Registry --> Ingest : spawn per\nPULL source
Ingest --> Remote : backfill + live tail
Ingest --> Manager : WriteEntry, tagged\nsource=<source ID>
PushHandlers --> Manager : WriteEntry, tagged\nsource=<client's tag>
Manager --> LogFile : append

note bottom of Mux
  Browser: GET /, /entries, /ws/entries, /sources, POST /sources, DELETE /sources/{id}
  Pusher:  POST /ingest (REST), GET /ws/ingest (WS), IngestService/Ingest (gRPC, h2c)
  Ops:     GET /healthz (no auth, not shown above)
end note

note bottom of Registry
  A Source is either:
  - **pull** (kind="pull", BaseURL+APIKey): logGO connects OUT via internal/ingest.
  - **push** (kind="push", Protocol only): no connection — just a reserved
    name/ID; a client pushes TO logGO tagged with that ID. Registering is a
    convenience (name + connection snippet), never enforced — an
    unregistered source still works, tagged under its raw string.
  A legacy sources.json from before "kind" existed has none — treated as pull.
end note

note bottom of PushHandlers
  Three protocols in, one path out: all three handlers call the same
  ingest() helper, which tags the source field and calls WriteEntry —
  see 06-push-ingestion-sequence.puml.
end note

note bottom of Ingest
  Pulling from conTogether (or anything similarly shaped) is a network
  *client* relationship only — neither project imports the other's code.
  See 05-ingestion-sequence.puml.
end note

note bottom of SourcesFile
  API keys live here in cleartext (0600
  perms) — the one place they're stored.
end note

@enduml
